From 0001-scheduler-unfair-boost Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: K80 Pro Power Optimizer
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] sched/eevdf: K80 Pro unfair scheduling for Android
 foreground tasks

Implement "unfair scheduling" for Android foreground tasks on the
EEVDF scheduler (kernel 6.6+), inspired by vivo OriginOS 3.0.

This patch:
  * Classifies tasks by their Android cpuset cgroup name
    (top-app / foreground / background / system-background / restricted).
  * Shortens the EEVDF deadline for top-app/foreground tasks during
    pick_eevdf() selection, making them selected earlier.
  * Lengthens the deadline for background tasks, delaying their execution.
  * Forces top-app wakeups to preempt running background tasks
    regardless of the default EEVDF preemption decision.

Design:
  * No Kconfig dependency -- built unconditionally via obj-y.
  * All new code lives in self-contained files.
  * Only 3 minimal hook points in fair.c:
      enqueue_task_fair()        - refresh task classification
      check_preempt_wakeup()     - force foreground preemption
      pick_eevdf()               - adjust deadline for selection
  * sysctl entries registered at runtime via register_sysctl().
  * RCU critical sections are balanced.
  * No use of removed symbols.

Works on any ARM64 kernel 6.6+ with CGROUPS + CPUSETS.

Signed-off-by: K80 Pro Power Optimizer
